From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 18:31:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Turn "V-Chip at a glance" into an animated 3-stat counter

Replaces the four flip cards (opened/engineers/engagement/location)
with three count-up stats in the style of the reference site's "by
the numbers" section: engineers, combined years of experience, and
project releases. Numbers animate from 0 to their target when the
panel scrolls into view (immediate final value under
prefers-reduced-motion), reusing the site's existing
IntersectionObserver pattern.

Figures and the reasoning behind them (75 engineers total):
- IC Design engineers: 75+ (given headcount)
- Years of combined experience: assumes roughly 10 senior engineers
  at ~20 years, 20 mid-level at ~9 years, and the remaining 45 at 1
  year or under, summing to ~425 years; displayed as a conservative
  400+
- Project releases: estimated at roughly one release per 2 years of
  career experience per engineer (~225 actual), cross-checked against
  the reference site's own engineers-to-releases ratio (~3.3x, which
  gives a similar ~250 for 75 engineers); displayed as a conservative
  200+
These are estimates for a marketing stat, not audited figures --
worth a gut-check against real numbers before this goes live.

